  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperation on Migration and Partnerships to Achieve Sustainable Solutions (COMPASS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme contributes to the protection and assistance of people on the move and decreased irregular migration. An ecological approach will be used to frame its overall response at the individual and household; community, and structural levels. Outcome 1 is delivering individual-level assistance to migrants and their families. Migrants eligible include victims of trafficking, smuggled migrants with identified protection needs, stranded migrants, migrants who have experienced or at risk of rights violations, violence, exploitation and/or abuse, and vulnerable migrant children. Outcome 2 will use innovative, experimental approaches to developing and implementing evidence-based community-level programming. Community level interventions will be comprised of i) building capacities of local officials and stakeholders to effectively manage migration in their communities; ii) increasing awareness of potential migrants and their families and communities on the risks of irregular migration and existing regular alternatives; iii) promoting sustainable reintegration. Outcome 3 will support and encourage structural-level interventions that enable migrant protection, address trafficking and smuggling, and support safe and dignified return and sustainable reintegration. Outcome 4 will assess the programme&apos;s impact on coordination, information sharing and learning.</narrative>
  </description>
